@startuml
title Plate - Multi-Tenant Social Fitness PWA Architecture

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam Padding 8

actor "User" as User

cloud "Cloudflare Edge" as Cloudflare {
  together {
    node "plate.example.com" as FrontendHost {
      component "Next.js + TypeScript PWA" as Frontend
    }

    node "api.plate.example.com" as GatewayHost {
      component "API Gateway Worker" as Gateway
    }
  }

  together {
    node "auth-api.plate.example.com" as AuthHost {
      component "Auth / Tenant Service\nCloudflare Worker" as AuthService
    }

    node "fitness-api.plate.example.com" as FitnessHost {
      component "Fitness Logging Service\nCloudflare Worker" as FitnessService
    }

    node "social-api.plate.example.com" as SocialHost {
      component "Social Feed Service\nCloudflare Worker" as SocialService
    }
  }
}

together {
  database "Supabase Auth DB\nPostgreSQL" as AuthDB
  database "Supabase Fitness DB\nPostgreSQL" as FitnessDB
  database "Supabase Social DB\nPostgreSQL" as SocialDB
}

storage "Supabase Storage\nMedia Files" as MediaStorage

User --> Frontend : Uses app

Frontend --> Gateway : HTTPS API requests

Gateway --> AuthService : /auth/*
Gateway --> FitnessService : /fitness/*
Gateway --> SocialService : /social/*

AuthService --> AuthDB : users\ntenants\nprofiles\nsettings

FitnessService --> FitnessDB : workouts\nexercises\nsets\nfood logs\nfood items

SocialService --> SocialDB : posts\nlikes\ncomments\nfollows

Frontend --> MediaStorage : Uploads and views media
SocialService --> MediaStorage : Store media URLs

AuthService ..> FitnessService : Validate user and tenant refs
AuthService ..> SocialService : Validate user and tenant refs
SocialService ..> FitnessService : Get workout and food summaries

note right of Frontend
PWA Features:
- Installable web app
- Mobile-first UI
- App manifest
- Service worker support
end note

note bottom of Gateway
Frontend only calls the API Gateway.
The gateway routes requests to the correct service.
end note

note bottom of AuthService
Each service is separately deployed
as a Cloudflare Worker.
end note

note bottom of AuthDB
Each service owns its own database.
No service directly queries another
service's database.
end note

@enduml
